1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,865
Thanks for making time.

2
00:00:01,865 --> 00:00:03,793
I'm really glad we're getting started.

3
00:00:03,793 --> 00:00:09,132
Before we dig into the details, let me give your team
a sense of who we are and what we're hoping to do

4
00:00:09,132 --> 00:00:09,841
together.

5
00:00:11,204 --> 00:00:14,930
We've been running these community health workshops
for going on six years.

6
00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:16,938
By most measures, they're doing well.

7
00:00:16,938 --> 00:00:21,803
Attendance is solid, the feedback forms come back
positive, we've built real relationships with the

8
00:00:21,803 --> 00:00:23,196
communities we serve.

9
00:00:23,196 --> 00:00:26,505
But our partner clinics have started raising something
with us.

10
00:00:26,678 --> 00:00:32,344
They're seeing that the people who come to our workshops
are learning the material in the room — they're engaged —

11
00:00:32,344 --> 00:00:36,733
but three months later, their actual health behaviors
haven't really shifted.

12
00:00:36,733 --> 00:00:40,065
So we know the workshops are working as workshops.

13
00:00:40,065 --> 00:00:43,965
The question we have is why the learning isn't translating
into change.

14
00:00:43,965 --> 00:00:45,685
And what we can do about it.

15
00:00:46,885 --> 00:00:52,178
So what we're hoping for from your team is a research-informed
set of recommendations.

16
00:00:52,178 --> 00:00:55,918
Look at what other organizations have tried with similar
programs.

17
00:00:55,918 --> 00:01:00,793
Dig into the research on health behavior change, especially
for the populations we serve.

18
00:01:00,793 --> 00:01:05,310
And come back to us with concrete suggestions we can
actually put into practice.

19
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:09,745
We don't need a hundred-page deliverable — honestly,
we wouldn't have the time to absorb that.

20
00:01:09,745 --> 00:01:14,772
What would really help is a focused analysis, with
clear, actionable recommendations.

21
00:01:14,772 --> 00:01:17,860
Something we can hand to our team and say, here's
where we're going.

22
00:01:19,061 --> 00:01:23,948
Timeline-wise, we have some flexibility, but let me
tell you what would be ideal.

23
00:01:23,948 --> 00:01:28,709
Our board meets in late April, and it would be really
nice to have something to share with them at that

24
00:01:28,709 --> 00:01:29,405
point.

25
00:01:29,405 --> 00:01:30,834
Even just a draft.

26
00:01:30,834 --> 00:01:33,307
That said, we're not setting that in stone.

27
00:01:33,307 --> 00:01:36,256
We'd rather you do good work than rush to make a date.

28
00:01:36,256 --> 00:01:40,459
On budget, this is going to need to be secondary research
and analysis.

29
00:01:40,459 --> 00:01:44,858
We just don't have the resources to fund interviews
or surveys of our participants.

30
00:01:44,858 --> 00:01:50,129
That said, we do have some internal survey data from
last year that we can share with you, if it would

31
00:01:50,129 --> 00:01:51,383
help your analysis.

32
00:01:52,583 --> 00:01:56,972
The last thing I'll share is just a bit about our
team and the people we serve.

33
00:01:56,972 --> 00:02:00,211
The workshops are run by our community health educators.

34
00:02:00,211 --> 00:02:05,923
There are eight of them, all incredibly dedicated,
and several of them are from the communities we serve.

35
00:02:05,923 --> 00:02:11,403
The curriculum itself was built in-house, four years
ago now, based on CDC guidance we were using at the

36
00:02:11,403 --> 00:02:12,040
time.

37
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,758
We haven't done a major refresh of it since.

38
00:02:14,758 --> 00:02:20,458
The one thing I really want you to keep in mind: our
participants come primarily from immigrant and refugee

39
00:02:20,458 --> 00:02:21,386
communities.

40
00:02:21,386 --> 00:02:25,438
So language access matters, and translation matters,
but it goes beyond that.

41
00:02:25,438 --> 00:02:28,120
Cultural context shapes everything we do.

42
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:32,555
How people understand health, who they trust, how
decisions get made in families.

43
00:02:32,555 --> 00:02:34,425
That's the world this work lives in.

44
00:02:35,625 --> 00:02:38,597
That's really the broad shape of it all, so I'll pause
there.

45
00:02:38,597 --> 00:02:43,334
Take your time digging in, and let's reconnect once
you've had a chance to look at the materials.

